A better scheduling question is: **Which activities require the same person or unique equipment, which activities must follow a preparation, rest, preheat, or cleanup period, which items must be held warm without blocking later work, and which finished components must all be ready before serving?** Applied here: the batter must rest 20 minutes before pancakes; the griddle must heat and then be cleaned before pancakes; bacon and pancake passes go into the warm oven; the plates must be warmed before service; coffee grinding begins 10 minutes after bacon starts; toast begins when the final pancake pass starts and must finish with its buttering; and serving waits for the eggs, buttered toast, and coffee. I added an inferred 10-minute oven preheat because the oven must be turned on and ready before plates or cooked food are held in it. The catalog tools and validation, analysis, and visualization tools are unavailable in this offline session, so no live URL, Gantt, or tool-generated itinerary can be returned.

